  "metadata": {
    "alignment": "standard",
    "description": "eugr's (Eugene Rakhmatulin) spark-vllm-docker recipe for Qwen's official Qwen3-Coder-Next-FP8 (block-wise FP8, Apache-2.0; checkpoint revision da6e2ed2, about 80 GB of weights) served by vLLM on two Sparks. Runs eugr's published vllm-node image (nightly-20260929, digest pinned; its build-metadata records spark-vllm-docker 42f62e34, vLLM 0.30.1rc1.dev336+gaf5b4857e and FlashInfer 4a638133) with upstream's launch: FlashInfer attention, FP8 KV cache, InstantTensor loading, prefix caching, qwen3_coder tool parsing, 131,072-token context and memory utilisation 0.8 (upstream defaults); upstream sets no mods, batched-token limit or sequence capacity, so those stay at vLLM's defaults. This is upstream's recipe as written (tensor parallel 2); the Controller runs it as native multi-node vLLM (eugr's default no-Ray cluster mode, instead of --distributed-executor-backend ray). No upstream performance claims are recorded. Upstream repository MIT. Physical Spark acceptance is pending.",
